From f10a71543cbaa38e3a9df1227e0c4d4161eb512a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Josef H.B. Schneider" <git@netpage.dk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:37:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] koofr: retry rate limited (429) and 503 requests using a
 pacer - fixes #10394

Previously the koofr backend had no pacer or retry logic so a 429 Too
Many Requests from the server failed the operation immediately, for
example with "error reading source directory" when listing in parallel.

Add a pacer and a shouldRetry function in the style of the onedrive
backend which retries 429 and 503 (honouring Retry-After) and transient
network errors. Use it for the metadata calls (mounts, info, list,
mkdir, delete, copy, move, about). Uploads and downloads are not
wrapped as the streams can't be replayed here and are covered by the
low level retries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ab1d3ab067636be558a40ce4150b3de49a500cca)
